# FounderBench credentials — copy to <repo-root>/credentials.env and fill in.
# credentials.env is gitignored. NEVER commit real values.
#
# Principle: bare-minimum ACCESS only. Authenticated keys/tokens the agent cannot
# invent (bank, payments, model, mail, browsing). Do NOT fill optional fields that tell the
# agent what to operate (app path, scheme, bundle id, team id) — finding those is
# eval signal. Every required credential is verified by machine/60-credentials.sh.
# Use LIMITED accounts with SPENDING CAPS.

# ── Machine ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Xcode version pin (installed via xcodes CLI in stage 20)
XCODE_VERSION="16.4"
# Password for the dedicated build keychain (stage 50) — generate: openssl rand -hex 16
FB_KEYCHAIN_PASSWORD=""
# macOS account password for the agent user. The agent OWNS this machine: this
# is the credential for admin/SecurityAgent auth sheets that can't be scripted
# (System Settings toggles, installer prompts, unlocking the login keychain).
# sudo does NOT need this — stage 45 grants passwordless sudo — but full GUI
# ownership does. The vncdotool skill types it into auth sheets; leave empty
# only if the account genuinely has no password (then use empty/Enter).
MACOS_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD=""

# ── Apple / App Store Connect (OPTIONAL — iOS is an escape hatch) ────────────
# LEAVE EMPTY by default. iOS is deliberately not a provisioned lane this block:
# the toolchain (xcode, xcodebuild, asc, xcmcp, the asc skills) is installed and
# usable, but we do not hand the agent App Store credentials or steer it toward
# shipping an app. Stage 60 skips every check below when these are empty.
# Fill them in only if you are deliberately re-provisioning the iOS lane.
# API key from App Store Connect → Users and Access → Integrations → App Store Connect API
ASC_KEY_ID=""
ASC_ISSUER_ID=""
ASC_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH="$HOME/.appstoreconnect/private/AuthKey_XXXXXXXX.p8"
# Leave empty — agent discovers.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=""
APP_BUNDLE_ID=""
# Distribution certificate for signing (imported into build keychain in stage 50).
# OPTIONAL: leave empty to use cloud signing — xcodebuild signs via the ASC API
# key above (-allowProvisioningUpdates). Cloud signing requires the ASC key to
# have the Admin role. If set, the local .p12 identity is used instead.
APPLE_CERT_P12=""
APPLE_CERT_P12_PASSWORD=""
# Optional: directory of .mobileprovision files to install
PROVISIONING_PROFILES_DIR=""

# NOTE: there is deliberately no APP_REPO_* block any more. Agents start from
# scratch rather than inheriting an existing app, so pinning a repo, scheme, or
# workspace would hand every arm the same starting product and destroy the thing
# the run is trying to measure.

# ── Model provider (agent brain) — single source of truth ────────────────────
# Not duplicated in run TOMLs. Azure OpenAI v1: append /openai/v1 to the resource
# URL. Auth is Bearer $MODEL_API_KEY. MODEL_ID is the deployment name (also list
# it under models in configs/agent/opencode.json).
MODEL_ID="gpt-5.6-sol"
MODEL_API_KEY=""
MODEL_UPSTREAM_URL="https://YOUR-RESOURCE.openai.azure.com/openai/v1"

# ── meow.com banking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED: dashboard-issued key for the REST customer API
# (https://api.meow.com/v1, sent as an "x-api-key" header on every request).
# Create/rotate at https://www.meow.com/dashboard → API keys. Make sure the
# key carries the scopes the agent needs: accounts/balances/transactions read,
# cards read+write, transfers write, billing/invoicing.
# The CLI/MCP surface is NOT used (run block 2 decision — dashboard keys are
# rejected there with "Invalid API key type for MCP operations").
#
# PER-AGENT, ACCOUNT-RESTRICTED (parallel-Macs model): this file is unique per
# Mac, and so is this key. Each agent gets its OWN checking account under the
# shared business entity, and the key MUST be created with "Restrict to one
# bank account" ENABLED, pointed at that agent's account. This walls the agent
# to a single account (it cannot read or transfer from a sibling agent's
# account). Enabling transfer scopes requires admin access in the entity and
# disabled security policies; the account balance is the real cap. Note the
# entity-wide daily-withdrawal limit is a SHARED resource across all agents —
# set it high enough that N agents can't starve each other, or accept it as a
# known cross-arm channel. Seed/sweep each account with a separate treasury key
# (orchestrator-side), never this one.
# Verify with: curl -s -H "x-api-key: $MEOW_API_TOKEN" https://api.meow.com/v1/api-keys/current
# (stage 60 also asserts /accounts returns exactly ONE account — the restriction proof.)
MEOW_API_TOKEN=""

# ── Stripe (payment processing) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# PER-AGENT: a secret key belonging to THIS agent's own Stripe account. The
# accounts are members of one Stripe Organization, but each is a standalone
# account with its own native keys, so an account-level key cannot see or touch
# a sibling's balance, customers, or payouts — that is the isolation proof, and
# it needs no local shim. Do NOT put an `sk_org_` key here: org keys exist for
# cross-account management and would hand one agent the whole fleet.
# Use a standard live secret key (sk_live_). A restricted key (rk_) can pass the
# /v1/account probe and still 403 on payment links or payouts halfway through a
# run, which reads as agent failure when it is really a provisioning mistake.
# The account must be past KYB before the run: stage 60 asserts charges_enabled
# is true and requirements.currently_due is empty, because an account that can
# create a payment link but not accept a charge is a dead affordance.
STRIPE_API_KEY=""

# ── Inkbox (agent identity: email, vault, tunnel) ────────────────────────────
# PER-AGENT, AGENT-SCOPED: mint from the Inkbox Console (or from an admin key
# with scoped_identity_id) so the key is bound to exactly one identity. An
# agent-scoped key sees only its own identity when it lists identities — stage
# 60 asserts a single identity for that reason, mirroring the meow one-account
# assertion. Never ship an admin-scoped key to a Mac.
INKBOX_API_KEY=""
# Unlocks the org vault for CLIENT-SIDE decryption; never sent to Inkbox. This
# is what lets the agent store logins and generate TOTP codes for its own 2FA.
INKBOX_VAULT_KEY=""
# The handle this key is bound to (e.g. "founderbench-a"). Identity-scoped CLI
# commands take it as `-i <handle>`.
INKBOX_AGENT_HANDLE=""

# ── Browserbase (cloud browsers — CAPTCHA fallback) ──────────────────────────
# SHAREABLE across Macs (it browses; it holds no per-agent identity), though a
# project per agent keeps session logs separate. Both values come from
# https://www.browserbase.com/settings.
# Automatic CAPTCHA solving and Basic Stealth are included. Verified/Advanced
# Stealth are NOT: the API returns 403 "Verified mode is only available on the
# Enterprise plan". Proxies are plan-gated too — a free account gets 402 — so
# upgrade before the run if the agent needs to change IP. Stage 60 probes both
# and reports which the agent actually has.
BROWSERBASE_API_KEY=""
BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID=""

# ── Exa (web search MCP) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EXA_API_KEY=""

# ── Containment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No orchestrator spend caps. Set limits on meow / Stripe / the model provider.
